{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109887","id":2767504538,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6k9MSa","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109887","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109887.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109887.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109887","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109887/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109887/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109887/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/0ad409bcd61de12523925686abfd853d435f1792","number":109887,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Rescale values to better utilize R128 range before snapping","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This is a further enhancement on top of PR #109100. Fixes #109852 and #107095.\r\n\r\nThis PR rescales values to better utilize R128's range before snapping. R128 is fixed-precision with 64 bits after the decimal point, but double already uses 53 of those, so a step size finer than 2^-11 will lose precision (2^-53 multiplied by 2^-11 is 2^-64 which is the limit of R128's fixed precision), and in practice even 1e-3 can be problematic. By rescaling the value and step, we can shift precision into the higher bits (effectively turning R128 into a makeshift float).\r\n\r\nIt seems that my initial declaration in PR #109100 that a 128-bit float was the ideal solution to the problem was actually correct, and we should really use such a thing once Godot upgrades to a C++ version where it's supported.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1332303119,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMzMyMzAzMTE5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/regression","name":"regression","description":"","color":"ff63ac","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12070367,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AuC3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/22","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/22","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/22/labels","number":22,"state":